course: dictionary
lesson: 11270
title: Wretched and its three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The best way to know which one is meant is to read the words around it. Wretched is one of these words. Look at how it is used: «I felt wretched with flu.»
explain: Here wretched means very unhappy or ill. You can check by swapping in a feeling word: I felt miserable with flu. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: The same word can also describe things that are very poor in quality: «They lived in wretched huts.» Huts are not feelings, so the clue is the word huts. Wretched here means very poor and bad.
explain: Sometimes people use wretched in a light, annoyed way: «This wretched computer won't work!» The speaker is cross, not swearing. Alice uses it in the same mild way: «three inches is such a wretched height to be.» She is unhappy about her height.
fact: Wretched is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a person, a hut or a computer.
fact: «Wretched» means very unhappy, ill or miserable, as in «I felt wretched with flu.»
fact: «Wretched» can also mean very poor or bad in quality, as in «wretched huts».
fact: In informal speech, «wretched» shows you are cross, as in «This wretched computer won't work!» It is mild, not a swear word.
fact: The noun wretch means a poor, unhappy person, and in the old hymn «Amazing Grace» the words «a wretch like me» mean a sinful, unhappy person.
exercise: «I felt wretched with flu.» What does wretched mean here? | *Very unhappy and ill | Very loud | Very clean and tidy | Very far away
exercise: «They lived in wretched huts.» What does wretched mean in this sentence? | Very happy and bright | *Very poor and bad in quality | Very new and shiny | Very tall and strong
exercise: «This wretched computer won't work!» How is the speaker feeling? | *Cross and annoyed | Excited and joyful | Sleepy and calm | Proud of the computer
test: Which word is the noun form of wretched? | *wretch | wrestle | wrench | wretchedly
test: Alice says «three inches is such a wretched height to be». What does wretched mean here? | Very ancient | Quite pleasant | Tall and proud | *Miserable, so Alice is unhappy about it
exam: In the old hymn «a wretch like me», what does wretch mean? | *A sinful, unhappy person | A happy singer | A small bird | A clean and tidy house
